<div id="A2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Below we provide more details about how we adapted these methods in our implementation.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1. </span>MiniLM</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We note that for this training procedure to work as proposed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2020</a>)</cite>, the number of attention heads
in the student and the teacher models have to match. This is not required by our loss (<a href="#S2.E3" title="In 2. Approach ‣ LEAF: Knowledge Distillation of Text Embedding Models with Teacher-Aligned Representations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Given the value vector <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{V}_{l,a}\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{V}_{l,a}\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times C}</annotation></semantics></math> for layer <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> and attention head <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> is the
sequence length and <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of channels in the value vector of attention <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>; typically, <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=d/A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=d/A</annotation></semantics></math>, where
<math id="A2.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> is the hidden dimension of the Transformer and <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of heads. We disregard the batch dimension in this analysis.
The <em id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">value relation matrix</em> <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{VR}_{l,a}\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>VR</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{VR}_{l,a}\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times T}</annotation></semantics></math> is then defined as</p>
<table id="A2.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{VR}_{l,a}=\mathrm{softmax}\left(\frac{\mathrm{V}_{l,a}\cdot\mathrm{V}_{l,a}^{\intercal}}{\sqrt{C}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>VR</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>⊺</mo></msubsup></mrow><msqrt><mi>C</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{VR}_{l,a}=\mathrm{softmax}\left(\frac{\mathrm{V}_{l,a}\cdot\mathrm{V}_{l,a}^{\intercal}}{\sqrt{C}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of transformer layers in the teacher and student models respectively. Then,</p>
<table id="A2.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{VR}}=\frac{1}{AT}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\sum_{a=1}^{A}\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{KL}}(\mathrm{VR}^{\tau}_{L,a}\left|\right|\mathrm{VR}^{\sigma}_{L^{\prime},a})_{t}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>VR</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>A</mi></munderover><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>VR</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>VR</mi><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mi>σ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{VR}}=\frac{1}{AT}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\sum_{a=1}^{A}\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{KL}}(\mathrm{VR}^{\tau}_{L,a}\left|\right|\mathrm{VR}^{\sigma}_{L^{\prime},a})_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{KL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{KL}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the KL-divergence between the value relation (<a href="#A2.E4" title="In B.1. MiniLM ‣ Appendix B Alternative Knowledge Distillation Approaches ‣ LEAF: Knowledge Distillation of Text Embedding Models with Teacher-Aligned Representations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) of the teacher <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> and
student <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>.
According to Eq. (<a href="#A2.E5" title="In B.1. MiniLM ‣ Appendix B Alternative Knowledge Distillation Approaches ‣ LEAF: Knowledge Distillation of Text Embedding Models with Teacher-Aligned Representations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>), loss is computed only for the last transformer layers of the respective networks <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, and averaged over the attention
heads and input tokens.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">An additional loss term is added to align the attention patterns of the two transformer backbones. Namely, let</p>
<table id="A2.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Att}_{l,a}=\mathrm{softmax}\left(\frac{\mathrm{K}_{l,a}\cdot\mathrm{Q}_{l,a}^{\intercal}}{\sqrt{C}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Att</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>⊺</mo></msubsup></mrow><msqrt><mi>C</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Att}_{l,a}=\mathrm{softmax}\left(\frac{\mathrm{K}_{l,a}\cdot\mathrm{Q}_{l,a}^{\intercal}}{\sqrt{C}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{K}_{l,a}\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{K}_{l,a}\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times C}</annotation></semantics></math> are the keys and <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Q}_{l,a}\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Q}_{l,a}\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times C}</annotation></semantics></math> are The
queries in head <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> of layer <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> of the transformer. <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Att}_{l,a}\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Att</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Att}_{l,a}\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times T}</annotation></semantics></math> is thus the attention
matrix in the given transformer head. Then, similarly to Eq.(<a href="#A2.E5" title="In B.1. MiniLM ‣ Appendix B Alternative Knowledge Distillation Approaches ‣ LEAF: Knowledge Distillation of Text Embedding Models with Teacher-Aligned Representations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>), we define</p>
<table id="A2.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(7)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{Att}}=\frac{1}{AT}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\sum_{a=1}^{A}\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{KL}}(\mathrm{Att}^{\tau}_{L,a}\left|\right|\mathrm{Att}^{\sigma}_{L^{\prime},a})_{t}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>Att</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>A</mi></munderover><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Att</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>Att</mi><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mi>σ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{Att}}=\frac{1}{AT}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\sum_{a=1}^{A}\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{KL}}(\mathrm{Att}^{\tau}_{L,a}\left|\right|\mathrm{Att}^{\sigma}_{L^{\prime},a})_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">as the KL-divergence between the student’s <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> and the teacher <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> attentions in the last transformer layer,
averaged over the attention heads and input tokens.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The loss we adopt to produce the results in Table <a href="#A2.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Appendix B Alternative Knowledge Distillation Approaches ‣ LEAF: Knowledge Distillation of Text Embedding Models with Teacher-Aligned Representations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> is then</p>
<table id="A2.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(8)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{MiniLM}}=\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{VR}}+\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{Att}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>MiniLM</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>VR</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>Att</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{MiniLM}}=\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{VR}}+\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{Att}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2. </span>TinyBERT</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">TinyBERT’s <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jiao et al., 2020</a>)</cite> proposed knowledge distillation scheme entails a soft cross-entropy loss between teacher and student output logits.
However, as remarked earlier, we discard the language modelling head in our architecture, and hence discard this loss component too.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We next discuss our implementation of the other loss components proposed in TinyBERT.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{l,t}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{l,t}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be the hidden state at the <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>-th layer and at the <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-th token.
As a convention, we denote <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{0,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{0,t}</annotation></semantics></math> as the hidden state before the first transformer layer; in BERT, <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{0,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{0,t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the
superposition of the input and positional embeddings.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To align hidden states, TinyBERT proposes the following loss:</p>
<table id="A2.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(9)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{Hidn}}=\frac{1}{TL}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\sum_{l=1}^{L^{\prime}}\mathrm{MSE}(h^{\tau}_{g(l),t}-W^{\mathrm{map}}h^{\sigma}_{l,t})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>Hidn</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munderover><mrow><mi>MSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mi>map</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>σ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{Hidn}}=\frac{1}{TL}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\sum_{l=1}^{L^{\prime}}\mathrm{MSE}(h^{\tau}_{g(l),t}-W^{\mathrm{map}}h^{\sigma}_{l,t}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:\mathbb{N}\rightarrow\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:\mathbb{N}\rightarrow\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> maps a hidden layer index in the student model to a corresponding hidden layer in the teacher and
is such that <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(L^{\prime})=L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(L^{\prime})=L</annotation></semantics></math>. As proposed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2020</a>)</cite>, we use <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(l)=\lfloor\frac{L}{L^{\prime}}\rfloor l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mfrac><mi>L</mi><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(l)=\lfloor\frac{L}{L^{\prime}}\rfloor l</annotation></semantics></math>.
<math id="A2.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\mathrm{map}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d^{\prime}\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mi>map</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\mathrm{map}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d^{\prime}\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> maps the student’s internal representations, which are often of smaller dimensions, into the teacher ones.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Similar to Section <a href="#A2.SS1" title="B.1. MiniLM ‣ Appendix B Alternative Knowledge Distillation Approaches ‣ LEAF: Knowledge Distillation of Text Embedding Models with Teacher-Aligned Representations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, TinyBERT also adopts a loss to align the attention patterns as follows:</p>
<table id="A2.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{Att}}=\frac{1}{AL}\sum_{a=1}^{A}\sum_{l=1}^{L^{\prime}}\mathrm{MSE}(\widetilde{\mathrm{Att}}^{\tau}_{g(l),a},\widetilde{\mathrm{Att}}^{\sigma}_{l,a})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>Att</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>A</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munderover><mrow><mi>MSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Att</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Att</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mi>σ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{Att}}=\frac{1}{AL}\sum_{a=1}^{A}\sum_{l=1}^{L^{\prime}}\mathrm{MSE}(\widetilde{\mathrm{Att}}^{\tau}_{g(l),a},\widetilde{\mathrm{Att}}^{\sigma}_{l,a}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathrm{Att}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>Att</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathrm{Att}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the attention matrix defined in Eq. (<a href="#A2.E6" title="In B.1. MiniLM ‣ Appendix B Alternative Knowledge Distillation Approaches ‣ LEAF: Knowledge Distillation of Text Embedding Models with Teacher-Aligned Representations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) but without <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{softmax(\cdot)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{softmax(\cdot)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Because of this loss component, TinyBERT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jiao et al., 2020</a>)</cite> requires the number of
heads in the student’s and teacher’s transformer layers to match, like with the MiniLM loss discussed in Section <a href="#A2.SS1" title="B.1. MiniLM ‣ Appendix B Alternative Knowledge Distillation Approaches ‣ LEAF: Knowledge Distillation of Text Embedding Models with Teacher-Aligned Representations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The aggregated loss we use to implement this knowledge distillation strategy is then</p>
<table id="A2.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(11)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{TinyBERT}}=\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{Hidn}}+\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{Att}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>TinyBERT</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>Hidn</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>Att</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{TinyBERT}}=\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{Hidn}}+\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{Att}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3. </span>DistilBERT</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">DistilBERT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sanh et al., 2020</a>)</cite> employes a combined loss on output logits and cosine similarity on internal
states. As before, we discard the loss on the logits because we do not have a language modelling head.
The paper does not specify how to compute the loss component related to the hidden states when the
number of layers do not match. The implementation at <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Face, 2023</a>)</cite> suggests that this
loss is only applied to the last layer. It also requires hidden state dimensions to match. We compensate
for this latter limitation by applying a linear map like in Eq. (<a href="#A2.E7" title="In B.1. MiniLM ‣ Appendix B Alternative Knowledge Distillation Approaches ‣ LEAF: Knowledge Distillation of Text Embedding Models with Teacher-Aligned Representations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We thus have</p>
<table id="A2.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(12)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{DistilBERT}}=-\mathrm{cos\_sim}(h^{\tau}_{L,t},W^{\mathrm{map}}h^{\sigma}_{L^{\prime},t})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>DistilBERT</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>sim</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mi>map</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>σ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{DistilBERT}}=-\mathrm{cos\_sim}(h^{\tau}_{L,t},W^{\mathrm{map}}h^{\sigma}_{L^{\prime},t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{cos\_sim}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>sim</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{cos\_sim}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is the vector cosine similarity.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>The Vocabulary  Dataset</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We took the list of 479k words from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kaggle, 2023</a>)</cite> and used Claude 3.5 Sonnet to produce definitions
and important facts about them using the prompt in Listing <a href="#LST1" title="Listing 1 ‣ Appendix C The Vocabulary Dataset ‣ LEAF: Knowledge Distillation of Text Embedding Models with Teacher-Aligned Representations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
Listing <a href="#LST2" title="Listing 2 ‣ Appendix C The Vocabulary Dataset ‣ LEAF: Knowledge Distillation of Text Embedding Models with Teacher-Aligned Representations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> shows some examples from this dataset.</p>
</div>
<figure id="LST1" class="ltx_float ltx_lstlisting">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float">Listing 1: </span>Prompt used to produce the <span id="LST1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">vocab</span> dataset.</figcaption>
<div id="LST1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle ltx_listing"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
<div id="lstnumberx1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">Please</span><span id="lstnumberx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">provide</span><span id="lstnumberx1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">ALL</span><span id="lstnumberx1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">the</span><span id="lstnumberx1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">definitions</span><span id="lstnumberx1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">and</span><span id="lstnumberx1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">,</span><span id="lstnumberx1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">if</span><span id="lstnumberx1.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">available</span><span id="lstnumberx1.17" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">,</span><span id="lstnumberx1.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.19" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">important</span><span id="lstnumberx1.20" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.21" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">facts</span><span id="lstnumberx1.22" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.23" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">about</span><span id="lstnumberx1.24" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.25" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">the</span><span id="lstnumberx1.26" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.27" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">following</span><span id="lstnumberx1.28" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.29" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">terms</span><span id="lstnumberx1.30" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">:</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx2" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">%</span><span id="lstnumberx3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">s</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx4" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx5" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">Provide</span><span id="lstnumberx5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">these</span><span id="lstnumberx5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">definitions</span><span id="lstnumberx5.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">/</span><span id="lstnumberx5.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">facts</span><span id="lstnumberx5.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">as</span><span id="lstnumberx5.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">a</span><span id="lstnumberx5.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">JSON</span><span id="lstnumberx5.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">document</span><span id="lstnumberx5.16" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">,</span><span id="lstnumberx5.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">formatted</span><span id="lstnumberx5.19" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.20" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">as</span><span id="lstnumberx5.21" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">:</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx6" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx7" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">"</span><span id="lstnumberx7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">word</span><span id="lstnumberx7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">":</span><span id="lstnumberx7.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">["</span><span id="lstnumberx7.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">definition</span><span id="lstnumberx7.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">or</span><span id="lstnumberx7.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">fact</span><span id="lstnumberx7.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">1",</span><span id="lstnumberx7.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">"</span><span id="lstnumberx7.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">definition</span><span id="lstnumberx7.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">or</span><span id="lstnumberx7.19" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.20" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">fact</span><span id="lstnumberx7.21" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.22" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">2",</span><span id="lstnumberx7.23" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.24" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">"</span><span id="lstnumberx7.25" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">definition</span><span id="lstnumberx7.26" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.27" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">or</span><span id="lstnumberx7.28" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.29" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">fact</span><span id="lstnumberx7.30" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.31" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">3",</span><span id="lstnumberx7.32" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.33" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">"</span><span id="lstnumberx7.34" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">definition</span><span id="lstnumberx7.35" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.36" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">or</span><span id="lstnumberx7.37" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.38" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">fact</span><span id="lstnumberx7.39" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.40" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">4",</span><span id="lstnumberx7.41" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.42" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">...]</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx8" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">}</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx9" class="ltx_listingline">
