<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Robustness Margins for <span id="A6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">leaf-mt</span></h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Section <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3. Robustness Margins ‣ 3. Results ‣ LEAF: Knowledge Distillation of Text Embedding Models with Teacher-Aligned Representations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> discusses our observed systems’ robustness to
the approximation error intorduced by our knowledge distillation scheme.
The robustness margin for <span id="A6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">leaf-mt</span> is shown in Figure <a href="#A6.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ Appendix F Robustness Margins for leaf-mt ‣ LEAF: Knowledge Distillation of Text Embedding Models with Teacher-Aligned Representations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>.
Note that the teacher model for <span id="A6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">leaf-mt</span>, mxbai-l-v1, does not output normalized vectors,
and as such the approximation error <math id="A6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> does not have an upper bound of 2.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.F11" class="ltx_figure" aria-describedby="acmlabel10">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F11.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 11</span>. </span><span id="A6.F11.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">NanoBEIR performance of various checkpoints stored while training <span id="A6.F11.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">leaf-mt</span>. Similar to the discussion in Section <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3. Robustness Margins ‣ 3. Results ‣ LEAF: Knowledge Distillation of Text Embedding Models with Teacher-Aligned Representations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>, we observe substantial robustness margins for this model.</span><span id="acmlabel10" class="ltx_acm_description ltx_centering ltx_nodisplay">X axis is approximation error and Y axis is nanobeir score. An horizontal line shows the performance of the target teacher model.
Circles show the performance of the checkpoint, they are below this horizontal target line. A linear fit of these circles is depicted.
The point where this linear fit meets the horizontal line determines the robustness margin.</span></figcaption><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.12539v1/robustness_margin_leaf_mt_after_1_epochs_only_and_up_to_30_epochs.svg" id="A6.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/340;" width="476" height="340"></object>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Inference Time Performance (CPU)</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Increasing inference throughput, lowering latencies, and operating on more economical infrastructure are typical core
goals of model distillation activities.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A7.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ Appendix G Inference Time Performance (CPU) ‣ LEAF: Knowledge Distillation of Text Embedding Models with Teacher-Aligned Representations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> reports our results for these key metrics of <span id="A7.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">leaf-ir</span> and <span id="A7.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">leaf-mt</span> when compared to their corresponding teachers.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The experiments are conducted on an AWS EC2 <code id="A7.p3.1.1" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">i3.large</code> instance, which is a commonly used CPU-only VM for database and search workloads.
These instances are equipped with 2 vCPUs and 15.25GB of RAM. Inference is performed on the ONNX Runtime.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A7.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A7.T8.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 8</span>. </span><span id="A7.T8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Performance comparison across different models. Max <math id="A7.T8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is the largest batch size that can be computed in 100ms or less; “-” indicates that no batch size can be computed within this time constraint.</span></figcaption>
